  "incident": {
    "symptom": "The renamed SRE team spends 78 percent of available time on tickets and manual recovery while a customer service has no user-journey SLO and sends sixty low-actionability pages per week.",
    "facts": [
      "The team name changed from operations to SRE but its authority, backlog and staffing did not.",
      "Manual worker restarts and copied access tickets grow with service demand.",
      "Developers do not participate in on-call or own production defects.",
      "There is no agreed user-journey SLO or error-budget policy.",
      "Sixty weekly pages have no measured precision, recall or actionability.",
      "One engineer is the only secondary escalation for three services."
    ],
